Package: tableonetoexcel
Title: Add Any Table to a Styled Excel Workbook
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Felippe", "Lazar", email = "felippelazarneto@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A workbook object that turns any table-like object (data
    frames, matrices, contingency tables, descriptive tables, gtsummary
    tables, survival fits, regression models, test results) into
    consistently styled Excel sheets (banded rows, auto column widths,
    readable labels) with one line per table.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.2.3
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    openxlsx2,
    R6,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    broom,
    broom.helpers,
    gtsummary,
    survival,
    tableone,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    tibble
Config/testthat/edition: 3
